Section 1: Initial Workspace Setup & Cleanup
Run these commands inside your PRoot Ubuntu terminal to ensure your environment dependencies and global runners are correctly installed.
1. Navigate to your project directory:
cd ~/Downloads/jhammerz_extracted

2. Install essential global tooling (tsx, pm2, serve):
npm install -g tsx pm2 serve

3. Clean-install local node dependencies bypassing version conflicts:
npm install --legacy-peer-deps

Section 2: Process Management & Persistence (pm2)
Manage and monitor background process daemons to keep your node alive continuously.
1. Launch the backend server in background mode:
npx pm2 start server.ts --name "aurelius-hub" --interpreter tsx

2. Check active process status:
pm2 status

3. View live background logs:
pm2 logs aurelius-hub

4. Restart or stop the backend daemon:
pm2 restart aurelius-hub
# To stop: pm2 stop aurelius-hub

5. Serve the frontend HUD interface statically (if not served via server.ts):
pm2 start npx --name "aurelius-ui" -- serve . -l 3000

Section 3: Edge Mesh & Network Testing
Verify off-grid peer-to-peer discovery and direct local socket bindings.
1. Identify your local subnet IP address:
ip addr show | grep -E 'inet '

(Note down your IP, e.g., 192.168.x.x)
2. Open a direct TCP mesh listener on Port 4080:
nc -lvnp 4080

3. Send a test packet from another local peer (Laptop/Phone on same Wi-Fi):
echo '{"peer_id":"node_02","status":"online"}' | nc <YOUR_PHONE_IP> 4080

4. Audit active listening ports on your device:
netstat -tuln | grep -E '3000|4080|3080|8080'

Section 4: Offline Local LLM Runtime Setup (llama.cpp)
Run on-device AI inference without external cloud API dependencies.
1. Install llama.cpp binary package:
pkg install llama.cpp -y

2. Download a lightweight quantized micro-model (e.g., Qwen2.5 0.5B Instruct GGUF):
curl -L -O https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-GGUF/resolve/main/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf

3. Launch the local LLM server on Port 8080:
llama-server --port 8080 -m qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf -c 2048 --host 0.0.0.0

4. Query your local on-device LLM via REST API:
curl http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions \
 -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
 -d '{
   "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Confirm sovereign status."}]
 }'

